[K2c THE INTERIOR CONTROL (D60's C7 excision, D66's `interior_of`) ON EVERY SWEPT RECORD, AT BOTH DEPTHS AND ON BOTH BAND COLUMNS — is any width or any band membership an ENDS artefact?]
  WHAT THE INTERIOR IS, AND IS NOT (round-1 MINOR 6).  `interior_of` returns the
  FULL closure and a SUBSET of events; `profile` then averages over that subset
  while every chart is still computed on the WHOLE record — a base at height
  hi - 3 still reads directions at hi - 1, inside the excised layers.  So the
  interior is a CONDITIONAL AVERAGE OVER A POPULATION OF EVENTS: not a record,
  not a sub-poset, and NOT AN OBJECT.  The word 'object' is withdrawn from
  every interior sentence in this unit.  For the same reason 'no wide chart is
  a boundary artefact' tests that the BASE is off the boundary; the chart's
  CONTENTS are not excised, and the gate says only what it measures.
